IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mtpd-dates`
IMPORT `mtpd-rules`
IMPORT `mtpd-seat`

-- Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016 (Vic) -- worked cases for the questions of the person whose treatment
-- it is (mtpd-seat.l4) and the date helpers.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- The deadline rules (ss 67(2), 88(3)) are tested through their exported questions, which run the DEONTIC rules by
-- EVALTRACE inside the helper's CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the person whose treatment it is`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

`no VCAT` MEANS `no VCAT order about its validity`
`no VCAT order` MEANS `no VCAT order about the appointment`
`MTDM` MEANS `an appointed medical treatment decision maker`
`SP` MEANS `a support person`
`me signing` MEANS `I signed it myself`
`ordinary` MEANS `ordinary medical treatment`
`no ID` MEANS `no relevant instructional directive`
`ID consents` MEANS `my instructional directive consents to it`
`ID refuses` MEANS `my instructional directive refuses it`
`undecided` MEANS `my decision maker has not decided yet`
`consents` MEANS `my decision maker consents`
`refuses` MEANS `my decision maker refuses`
`treatment` MEANS `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`
`interstate ACD` MEANS `an advance care directive made in another State or Territory`
`interstate appointment` MEANS `an appointment of a decision maker or support person made in another State or Territory`
`all of it` MEANS `everything in it could validly have been given under this Act`
`part of it` MEANS `only part of it could validly have been given under this Act`
`none of it` MEANS `none of it could validly have been given under this Act`
`penalty` MEANS `What is the maximum penalty for an offence against me`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 2 2028) `to` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 2 2027) `to` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the date` 14 `days after` (`d` 20 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 5 3 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 15 12 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 1 2028

§§ `s 4 -- do I have decision-making capacity`

-- Arguments: age, evidence of incapacity, understand, retain, use or weigh, communicate.
-- An adult of exactly 18 with no evidence to the contrary is presumed to have capacity, whatever the abilities stated.
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as an adult I am presumed to have it, and there is no evidence to the contrary (s 4(2))`
-- A child of 17 has no presumption: the four abilities decide.
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 17 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I can understand, retain, use and weigh, and communicate, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (4)(d))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 17 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`
-- With evidence to the contrary, an adult is tested like anyone else.
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 80 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I can understand, retain, use and weigh, and communicate, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (4)(d))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 80 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` 80 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`

§§ `s 3 -- who may apply to VCAT (eligible applicant)`

-- Finding 3: the person concerned is not on the list.
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `me, the person whose treatment, directive or appointment it is` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `a health practitioner who has my care or is treating me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `my medical treatment decision maker` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `my support person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `the Public Advocate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `someone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in my affairs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply to VCAT about me` `anyone else (a relative or friend VCAT has not found to have a special interest)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 13, 14, 16, 17, 21, 22 -- is my advance care directive valid`

-- Arguments: age, capacity and understanding, writing with details, signer, number of adult witnesses, signed and dated
-- together, a registered medical practitioner witness with qualification written, a witness is my appointed decision
-- maker, a witness with prescribed training (children), certifications, induced, VCAT order.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `an adult who is not a witness signed it at my direction` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
-- Each requirement missed in turn.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 FALSE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: I lacked capacity for, or did not understand, a statement in it (s 13(a), s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE FALSE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: it is not in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address (s 16(1)(a), (b), s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `someone else signed it at my direction (a child, a witness, or for an appointment an appointee)` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: it was not properly signed (s 16(1)(c), (2), s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `nobody signed it` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: it was not properly signed (s 16(1)(c), (2), s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnesses did not certify as s 17(2) and (3) require (s 21(1))`
-- A child of 17 needs a witness with the prescribed training; at 18 it is not needed.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 17 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 17 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 18 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
-- The first failure in the order of the Act is reported.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 FALSE FALSE `nobody signed it` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no VCAT` EQUALS `no effect as a directive: I lacked capacity for, or did not understand, a statement in it (s 13(a), s 21(1))`
-- VCAT's orders; inducement makes it void whatever VCAT declared.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply` EQUALS `valid: VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply (s 22(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply` EQUALS `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `VCAT declared it invalid` EQUALS `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 22(2)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no VCAT` EQUALS `void: I was induced to give it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 14(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive valid` 30 TRUE TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply` EQUALS `void: I was induced to give it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 14(2))`

§§ `ss 19, 20, 22 -- is my advance care directive in force`

-- Arguments: signed on, states an expiry date, expiry date, revocation, revoked on, suspended, the day asked about.
-- Signed 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `not yet in force: it has not been signed in accordance with Part 2 by that day (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `in force (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2045) EQUALS `in force (s 19)`
-- Expiry 1 January 2030: in force on 31 December 2029, not on 1 January 2030 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE (`d` 31 12 2029) EQUALS `in force (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `no longer in force: its expiry date has been reached (s 19(2)(a))`
-- Revoked by a later directive on 10 June 2026: in force the day before, not on the day.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `revoked by a later advance care directive I gave (s 20(3))` (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 9 6 2026) EQUALS `in force (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `revoked by a later advance care directive I gave (s 20(3))` (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `revoked by a revocation made with the formalities of Part 2 (s 20(1))` (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `revoked in whole by VCAT (s 22(2)(a)(i))` (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`
-- A revocation date with no revocation is ignored.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `not revoked` (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `in force (s 19)`
-- Suspension, and revocation over suspension.
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `not revoked` (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `suspended by VCAT for that day (s 22(2)(a)(iii))`
#ASSERT `Is my advance care directive in force` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) `revoked by a later advance care directive I gave (s 20(3))` (`d` 10 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`

§§ `ss 6, 8A, 12, 18 -- what is this statement in my directive`

-- Arguments: subject, expressly instructional, clear, interstate, unlawful, breach of standards, prescribed.
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an instructional directive: it takes effect as if I had consented to or refused the treatment myself (s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `consent to a special medical procedure` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `palliative care` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `voluntary assisted dying` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not authorised by this Act: voluntary assisted dying (s 8A)`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void and severed from the directive: an unlawful or prohibited statement (s 18(2))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `void and severed from the directive: an unlawful or prohibited statement (s 18(2))`
#ASSERT `What is this statement in my advance care directive` `treatment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `void and severed from the directive: an unlawful or prohibited statement (s 18(2))`

§§ `ss 95-97 -- is my interstate instrument recognised`

-- Finding 2: a recognised interstate directive's statements are values directives.
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate ACD` TRUE `all of it` EQUALS `recognised: taken to be an advance care directive under this Act, but its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii))`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate ACD` TRUE `part of it` EQUALS `recognised in part, to the extent it could have been given under this Act; its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii), 97)`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate ACD` TRUE `none of it` EQUALS `not recognised as a directive, but it may be considered as my preferences and values (s 95(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate ACD` FALSE `all of it` EQUALS `not recognised as a directive, but it may be considered as my preferences and values (s 95(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate appointment` TRUE `all of it` EQUALS `recognised: taken to be an appointment under Part 3 (s 96(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate appointment` TRUE `part of it` EQUALS `recognised in part, to the extent the powers could have been given under Part 3 (ss 96(1), 97)`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate appointment` TRUE `none of it` EQUALS `not covered: s 96 recognises it only if it complies with the law where it was made and to the extent Part 3 allows`
#ASSERT `Is my interstate instrument recognised in Victoria` `interstate appointment` FALSE `all of it` EQUALS `not covered: s 96 recognises it only if it complies with the law where it was made and to the extent Part 3 allows`

§§ `ss 26-45 -- is my appointment valid`

-- Arguments: kind, my age, capacity, appointee's age, writing with details, signer, number of adult witnesses, together,
-- authorised witness with qualification, a witness is an appointee, certifications, accepted, induced, VCAT order.
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `made, but not yet in effect: each appointee must first accept it in writing (ss 28(1)(g), 29, 33(f), 34)`
-- Ages at the edge: 18 and 18 are fine; 17 on either side is outside s 26(1).
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 18 TRUE 18 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 17 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not covered: the Act gives this power only to an adult with capacity appointing an adult (s 26(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 17 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not covered: the Act gives this power only to an adult with capacity appointing an adult (s 26(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 FALSE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not covered: the Act gives this power only to an adult with capacity appointing an adult (s 26(1))`
-- A support person: a child may appoint a child.
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `SP` 15 TRUE 12 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `SP` 40 FALSE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not covered: the Act gives this power only to a person with capacity (s 31(1))`
-- Formal failures (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 FALSE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: it is not in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details (s 28(1)(a)-(c), s 33(a)-(c))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `someone else signed it at my direction (a child, a witness, or for an appointment an appointee)` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: it was not properly signed (ss 28(1)(d), 33(d), 37)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `an adult who is not a witness signed it at my direction` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: the witnessing did not meet s 36(1)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: the witnessing did not meet s 36(1)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: the witnessing did not meet s 36(1)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: the witnesses did not certify as s 36(2) requires`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `not validly made: the witnesses did not certify as s 36(2) requires`
-- Inducement: void for a decision maker (s 42(2)); no such rule for a support person (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `void: I was induced to make it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 42(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `SP` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `no VCAT order` EQUALS `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `VCAT declared the attempt to appoint effective (ss 43(2)(b)(ii), 45)` EQUALS `void: I was induced to make it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 42(2))`
-- VCAT's orders.
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `MTDM` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `VCAT declared the attempt to appoint effective (ss 43(2)(b)(ii), 45)` EQUALS `effective: VCAT declared it effective despite non-compliance (s 45)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment valid` `SP` 40 TRUE 35 TRUE `me signing` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `VCAT declared the appointment invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))` EQUALS `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))`

§§ `ss 30, 35, 38, 39 -- is my appointment in force`

-- Arguments: kind, my revocation, later support person appointed, resignation, VCAT revoked.
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I have not revoked it` FALSE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `in force (s 38)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I revoked it with capacity and with the formalities of s 28(1) or s 33` FALSE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `revoked by me (ss 30, 35(1), 38(2)(a))`
-- A later support person revokes an earlier support person, not a decision maker.
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I have not revoked it` TRUE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `in force (s 38)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `SP` `I have not revoked it` TRUE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `revoked by my later appointment of a support person (s 35(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `SP` `I have not revoked it` FALSE `the appointee resigned in writing, signed, dated and witnessed by one adult (s 39(4))` FALSE EQUALS `ended: the appointee resigned (ss 38(2)(b), 39)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I have not revoked it` FALSE `the appointee said they resign, without meeting s 39(4)` FALSE EQUALS `in force (s 38)`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I tried to revoke it without capacity for that decision` FALSE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `in force: my attempted revocation was without capacity, so s 30 or s 35(1) does not let me revoke it`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `SP` `I tried to revoke it without the formalities` FALSE `the appointee has not resigned` FALSE EQUALS `in force: my attempted revocation lacked the formalities, unless VCAT declares it effective (s 43(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Is my appointment in force` `MTDM` `I have not revoked it` FALSE `the appointee has not resigned` TRUE EQUALS `revoked by VCAT (s 43(2)(a)(i))`

§§ `s 55 -- who is my medical treatment decision maker`

-- Arguments: age, mental health patient, appointee, VCAT guardian, spouse or partner, primary carer, adult child, parent,
-- adult sibling (each: in a close and continuing relationship and reasonably available, willing and able).
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my appointed medical treatment decision maker: the first listed appointee who is reasonably available and willing and able (ss 28(2), 55(1))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my guardian appointed by VCAT with power to make medical treatment decisions (s 55(2))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my spouse or domestic partner (s 55(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my primary carer (s 55(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my oldest adult child who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(i))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my oldest parent who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my oldest adult sibling who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(iii))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 55 does not apply while I am a mental health patient (s 55(5)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
-- A child of 17: a parent (or guardian or person with parental responsibility) only; a partner does not count.
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 17 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my parent, guardian or other person with parental responsibility for me (s 55(4))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`
-- At 18, a parent comes only after partner, carer and adult child.
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my oldest parent who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my spouse or domestic partner (s 55(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `there is a medical treatment decision maker` (`Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `there is a medical treatment decision maker` (`Who is my medical treatment decision maker` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

