#ASSERT `Is this significant treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this significant treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this significant treatment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this significant treatment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this significant treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Part 4 -- may I be given this treatment while I lack capacity`

-- Arguments: capacity, mental health patient, kind, intrusion, risk, side effects, distress, likely to recover, delay
-- worsens, directive located, instructional directive, changed circumstances, VCAT delay worsens, clinically appropriate,
-- decision maker located, decision, Public Advocate consents.
-- Routine treatment, nothing located: may be given without consent.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `yes, without consent: routine treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` TRUE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for this decision, so the decision is mine`
-- Kinds with their own rules.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE TRUE `treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not this Part: Part 4 does not apply to treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient, or to neurosurgery for mental illness (s 48(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `neurosurgery for mental illness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not this Part: Part 4 does not apply to treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient, or to neurosurgery for mental illness (s 48(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `a special medical procedure` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `not this Division: a special medical procedure is dealt with under Part 6 of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (s 57(2))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `palliative care` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID refuses` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `refuses` FALSE EQUALS `palliative care: it may be given despite my decision maker's decision, with regard to my preferences and values and after consulting my decision maker (s 54)`
-- Significant treatment, nothing located: only with the Public Advocate's consent.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `only if the Public Advocate consents: significant treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` TRUE EQUALS `yes: significant treatment the Public Advocate has consented to (s 63(1)(b), (2))`
-- Finding 4: a mental health patient needing physical treatment, nothing located.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: I am a mental health patient, so s 63 does not apply (s 63(3)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
-- Fork F6: a directive with values only and no decision maker.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: I have a directive with no relevant instructional directive and no decision maker was found; s 63 speaks only where neither is located`
-- An instructional directive refusing the treatment binds (even over a decision maker's consent), unless s 51's two
-- beliefs are both held.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID refuses` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `no: my instructional directive refuses it, and it must be withheld or withdrawn (s 60(1)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID refuses` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: my instructional directive refuses it, and it must be withheld or withdrawn (s 60(1)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID refuses` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: my instructional directive refuses it, and it must be withheld or withdrawn (s 60(1)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID refuses` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `the practitioner may refuse to follow my instructional directive's refusal (s 51)`
-- An instructional directive consenting: given if clinically appropriate.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID consents` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my instructional directive consents and the practitioner thinks it clinically appropriate (s 60(1)(a)(ii))`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ID consents` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `my instructional directive consents, but the practitioner need not give it: not clinically appropriate (ss 8, 60(1)(a)(ii))`
-- No relevant instructional directive: my decision maker decides.
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 61)`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `refuses` FALSE EQUALS `no: my medical treatment decision maker refuses (ss 58, 61)`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `undecided` TRUE EQUALS `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 60(1)(b), 61)`
-- Likely to recover within a reasonable time (s 59), before s 60 and s 63 (fork F7).
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `yes, before I recover: my directive or my decision maker consents and delay would significantly worsen my condition (s 59)`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `no: not before I recover capacity, which is likely within a reasonable time (s 59)`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ID consents` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `yes, before I recover: my directive or my decision maker consents and delay would significantly worsen my condition (s 59)`
#ASSERT `May I be given this treatment while I lack capacity` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no ID` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: not before I recover capacity, which is likely within a reasonable time (s 59)`

§§ `s 53 -- emergencies`

-- Arguments: ECT, save life, prevent serious damage, prevent significant pain or distress, refusal known.
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds it is urgently necessary (s 53(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds it is urgently necessary (s 53(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds it is urgently necessary (s 53(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 53 does not apply, as the practitioner does not believe it urgently necessary for any of its purposes (s 53(1))`
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the practitioner knows I have refused this treatment (s 53(2))`
#ASSERT `May I be treated without consent in an emergency` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by s 53: electroconvulsive treatment is excluded from it (s 53(1))`

§§ `ss 62, 67 -- the Public Advocate`

#ASSERT `Must my practitioner notify the Public Advocate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my practitioner notify the Public Advocate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my practitioner notify the Public Advocate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 14 days after notification: 1 February 2028 -> 15 February; 20 February 2028 (leap year) -> 5 March; 2027 -> 6 March.
#ASSERT `By when must the Public Advocate apply to VCAT` (`d` 1 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 15 2 2028
#ASSERT `By when must the Public Advocate apply to VCAT` (`d` 20 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 5 3 2028
#ASSERT `By when must the Public Advocate apply to VCAT` (`d` 20 2 2027) EQUALS `d` 6 3 2027
-- Arguments: unreasonable, notified on, applied, applied on, today.
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` FALSE (`d` 1 2 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 2 2028) (`d` 1 5 2028) EQUALS `no duty to apply: the Public Advocate does not think the refusal unreasonable, and must tell the practitioner so (s 67(1))`
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) (`d` 1 5 2028) EQUALS `applied in time (s 67(2))`
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 1 5 2028) EQUALS `applied in time (s 67(2))`
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 16 2 2028) (`d` 1 5 2028) EQUALS `late: the 14 days after notification have passed (s 67(2))`
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `still in time: the Public Advocate must apply by the last day (s 67(2))`
#ASSERT `Where does the Public Advocate's review stand` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 2 2028) EQUALS `late: the 14 days after notification have passed (s 67(2))`

§§ `ss 49, 52 -- is the practitioner protected from my claim`

-- Arguments: good faith, without negligence, believed Part 4 complied with, reliance, believed in accordance.
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the practitioner did not rely on an instructional directive` FALSE EQUALS `protected under s 52(1): not liable in any civil proceeding (or for an offence, unprofessional conduct or a code breach)`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force` TRUE EQUALS `protected under s 52(2): acted on my instructional directive; not liable in any civil proceeding because of that treatment or its withholding`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE `relied on my instructional directive, which had been revoked or was invalid, without knowing` TRUE EQUALS `protected under s 52(2): acted on my instructional directive; not liable in any civil proceeding because of that treatment or its withholding`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE `relied on my instructional directive, knowing it had been revoked or was invalid` TRUE EQUALS `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force` FALSE EQUALS `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the practitioner did not rely on an instructional directive` FALSE EQUALS `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force` TRUE EQUALS `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`
#ASSERT `Is the practitioner protected from my claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force` TRUE EQUALS `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`

§§ `Part 5 -- research procedures`

-- Arguments: age, capacity, approved, likely to recover, instructional directive, has decision maker, decision, Division 3 met.
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 TRUE TRUE FALSE `no ID` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for it, so it needs my own consent`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 17 FALSE TRUE FALSE `ID consents` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 5 applies only to adults (s 72(1))`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE `ID consents` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: the research project has not been approved by its human research ethics committee (ss 75(a), 84)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE `ID consents` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: I am likely to recover capacity in time, so it must not be given under Part 5 (s 72(2))`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 18 FALSE TRUE FALSE `ID consents` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I consented to it in an instructional directive (s 75(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `ID refuses` TRUE `consents` TRUE EQUALS `no: my instructional directive refuses it, so there is no consent under s 75(b)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ID` TRUE `consents` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consented (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ID` TRUE `refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no: my medical treatment decision maker refused (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ID` TRUE `undecided` TRUE EQUALS `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ID` FALSE `undecided` TRUE EQUALS `yes, without consent: authorised under Part 5 Division 3 (ss 75(b)(iii), 80)`
#ASSERT `May a research procedure be given to me` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ID` FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `no: no consent and not authorised under Division 3 (ss 75, 85)`

§§ `s 88 -- rehearings`

#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `a final order made at first instance` EQUALS `yes, as a party at first instance (s 88(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was given notice of the hearing but was not a party` `a final order made at first instance` EQUALS `yes, with VCAT's leave, as a person given notice (s 88(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was neither a party nor given notice` `a final order made at first instance` EQUALS `not covered: s 88(1) gives the right only to a party or a person given notice`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `an interim or temporary order` EQUALS `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `an order on an application to suspend or revoke the appointment of a decision maker or support person` EQUALS `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `an order on an application under Part 5 Division 4 (medical research)` EQUALS `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `an order made by VCAT constituted by the President` EQUALS `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a rehearing` `I was a party at first instance` `an order on an application for a rehearing or for leave` EQUALS `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
-- 28 days after the day of the order: 1 March 2027 -> 29 March 2027; written reasons given 10 March 2027 -> 7 April 2027;
-- 1 February 2028 -> 29 February 2028 (leap year); 1 February 2027 -> 1 March 2027.
